# Copy to `.github/CODEOWNERS` and replace every handle before it does anything.
#
# It ships as a sample for the same reason `env_config/*/dart_defines.json`
# does: the real file needs values this base cannot know. And unlike a wrong
# URL, a wrong CODEOWNERS fails *silently* — GitHub cannot request review from a
# team that does not exist, so the file sits there looking like review coverage
# while every PR merges unreviewed. That is the failure this repo's own rules
# call out: do not assert a guarantee you have not implemented.
#
# Ownership below is by architectural layer, not by directory convenience. The
# packages that everything else depends on get the most eyes, because a mistake
# in `core_kit` reaches every screen in the app and a mistake in a feature does
# not.

# Default. Everything not matched below.
*                           @your-org/mobile

# The layer graph itself. A change here re-shapes what every package may import,
# and `make check-deps` will happily enforce a rule that was widened by mistake.
/tools/                     @your-org/mobile-leads
/Makefile                   @your-org/mobile-leads
/.github/                   @your-org/mobile-leads
/analysis_options.yaml      @your-org/mobile-leads

# Foundations: pure Dart contracts and the base classes every feature extends.
# `core_kit` never imports Flutter, and that is easy to break in a hurry.
/core/core_kit/             @your-org/mobile-leads
/core/core_arch/            @your-org/mobile-leads

# Security-relevant surface. Token storage, the 401 refresh path, the
# interceptor chain, the log redactor's blast radius.
/core/core_storage/         @your-org/mobile-leads @your-org/security
/core/core_network/         @your-org/mobile-leads @your-org/security
/features/feature_auth/     @your-org/mobile-leads @your-org/security

# Design system. A token change is an app-wide visual change.
/core/core_ui/              @your-org/mobile @your-org/design

# The composition root: DI, router, shell, session.
/app/lib/app/di/            @your-org/mobile-leads
/app/lib/app/router/        @your-org/mobile-leads

# Decisions, not code. Changing an ADR changes what the next person is allowed
# to do, so it is reviewed by whoever has to live with it.
/docs/adr/                  @your-org/mobile-leads
/CLAUDE.md                  @your-org/mobile-leads
